    <node id="sym:repo2graph/cli.py::_utf8_stdio">
      <data key="d0">sym:repo2graph/cli.py::_utf8_stdio</data>
      <data key="d1">symbol</data>
      <data key="d2">_utf8_stdio</data>
      <data key="d10">_utf8_stdio</data>
      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">repo2graph/cli.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">1200</data>
      <data key="d13">1220</data>
      <data key="d14">def _utf8_stdio() -&gt; None:</data>
      <data key="d15">Make a redirected or piped stdout/stderr UTF-8.

    A Windows pipe or file gets the ANSI code page (cp1252), so `repo2graph
    rag ... &gt; pack.md` over a repository holding `こんにちは` wrote `?????` --
    `_emit` kept it from crashing, but the text was gone. A console is left
    alone (Python already writes it as UTF-16), and so is an explicit
    PYTHONIOENCODING: that is the user choosing the encoding, and the
    "Windows CP1252" CI job relies on it to exercise `_emit`'s fallback.</data>
      <data key="d_nodegraphics">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="5036.97" y="797.00" width="116.25" height="32.50" />
          <y:Fill color="#57C7E3" transparent="false" />
          <y:BorderStyle color="#4a4f57" type="line" width="1.0" />
          <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" fontSize="11" textColor="#1c2330" visible="true">_utf8_stdio</y:NodeLabel>
          <y:Shape type="ellipse" />
        </y:ShapeNode>
      </data>
    </node>
