    <node id="sym:repo2graph/doctor.py::check_tree_sitter">
      <data key="d0">sym:repo2graph/doctor.py::check_tree_sitter</data>
      <data key="d1">symbol</data>
      <data key="d2">check_tree_sitter</data>
      <data key="d10">check_tree_sitter</data>
      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">repo2graph/doctor.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">232</data>
      <data key="d13">296</data>
      <data key="d14">def check_tree_sitter() -&gt; CheckResult:</data>
      <data key="d15">Check that grammars actually *load*, not merely that they are configured.

    This used to report `len(LANG_CFG)` grammars "configured" and return "ok".
    `LANG_CFG` is a dict literal in `parse.py`, so the count was a property of the
    source code and the check could not fail for the thing it was named after: with
    every grammar unloadable, doctor still said ok and `build` still exited 0 with an
    empty graph. `parser_for()` swallows LookupError/ValueError/ImportError/
    AttributeError and returns None, so "no grammar" and "nothing to parse" are
    indistinguishable downstream unl</data>
