    <node id="sym:repo2graph/embed.py::write_vectors">
      <data key="d0">sym:repo2graph/embed.py::write_vectors</data>
      <data key="d1">symbol</data>
      <data key="d2">write_vectors</data>
      <data key="d10">write_vectors</data>
      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">repo2graph/embed.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">198</data>
      <data key="d13">241</data>
      <data key="d14">def write_vectors(
    path: str | Path,
    vectors: dict[str, list[float]],
    model_id: str,
    dim: int,
    chunk_ids: Iterable[str],
    text_hashes: Iterable[str] | None = None,
    build_id: str | None = None,
) -&gt; int:</data>
      <data key="d15">Write vectors.npy plus its sibling vectors.meta.json; return the count.

    Row order is `chunk_ids` order, which is chunks.jsonl order, so re-running
    `embed` over an unchanged index reproduces the file byte for byte.

    `build_id` is the manifest build_id for the index these vectors were built
    against; stored so `verify_artifacts` and `doctor` can detect when a rebuild
    has produced a new manifest build_id but `embed` has not been re-run.</data>
      <data key="d_nodegraphics">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="5788.82" y="886.00" width="179.22" height="43.55" />
