    <node id="sym:repo2graph/fetch.py::_auth_env">
      <data key="d0">sym:repo2graph/fetch.py::_auth_env</data>
      <data key="d1">symbol</data>
      <data key="d2">_auth_env</data>
      <data key="d10">_auth_env</data>
      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">repo2graph/fetch.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">178</data>
      <data key="d13">211</data>
      <data key="d14">def _auth_env(token: str | None) -&gt; dict[str, str]:</data>
      <data key="d15">Environment carrying the clone credential out of band.

    The token must never be an argv element: it would be visible in
    `ps`/`/proc` to every other user. git reads http.extraheader from
    GIT_CONFIG_* for this one invocation only, so nothing lands on disk either.

    Also strips `GIT_DIR`/`GIT_WORK_TREE`/`GIT_INDEX_FILE` inherited from the
    ambient environment, so they cannot override the explicit `-C &lt;target&gt;`
    every call site here passes.</data>
      <data key="d_nodegraphics">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="4306.65" y="1052.30" width="114.55" height="37.70" />
          <y:Fill color="#57C7E3" transparent="false" />
          <y:BorderStyle color="#4a4f57" type="line" width="1.0" />
          <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" fontSize="11" textColor="#1c2330" visible="true">_auth_env</y:NodeLabel>
          <y:Shape type="ellipse" />
        </y:ShapeNode>
      </data>
    </node>
