      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">93</data>
      <data key="d13">101</data>
      <data key="d14">def sniff_header_lang(raw: bytes) -&gt; str:</data>
      <data key="d15">Guess "c" or "cpp" for a `.h` file from its content (#377).

    Cheap and best-effort: any single C++ signal anywhere in `raw` wins,
    since a plain C header contains none of `CPP_HEADER_HINTS` in ordinary
    (non-comment, non-string) code. Callers pass the bytes they already read
    for hashing/parsing -- this never opens the file itself.</data>
