      <data key="d0">sym:repo2graph/tasks.py::TaskManager</data>
      <data key="d1">symbol</data>
      <data key="d2">TaskManager</data>
      <data key="d10">TaskManager</data>
      <data key="d11">class</data>
      <data key="d3">repo2graph/tasks.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">105</data>
      <data key="d13">222</data>
      <data key="d14">class TaskManager:</data>
      <data key="d15">Owns at most one in-flight build per index directory.

    One per directory, not one per request: two concurrent builds writing the
    same artifacts would race each other through `atomic_write`, and the loser's
    partial work would be silently discarded. A second request for a directory
    already building joins the existing task instead of starting another.

    Args:
        builder: Callable taking `(repo, out)` that performs the build. Injected
            so tests need not parse a real repository.
        estimator: Callable taking `repo` and returning an estimated duration in
     </data>
      <data key="d_nodegraphics">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="6928.38" y="1656.45" width="127.88" height="35.75" />
          <y:Fill color="#57C7E3" transparent="false" />
