      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">164</data>
      <data key="d13">180</data>
      <data key="d14">def _evict_locked(self) -&gt; None:</data>
      <data key="d15">Drop the oldest finished tasks once `_by_id` exceeds MAX_TRACKED_TASKS.
        Caller must hold self._lock.

        A task still BUILDING is skipped rather than evicted -- an in-flight
        build must always remain pollable -- so if enough builds are running
        concurrently, `_by_id` can briefly stay above the cap; it shrinks back
        as soon as those tasks finish and a new one triggers eviction again.</data>
      <data key="d_nodegraphics">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="398.90" y="1738.95" width="139.15" height="29.90" />
