      <data key="d14">def test_the_skip_does_not_consume_the_node(alias_index: Index) -&gt; None:</data>
      <data key="d15">Skipping an alias as a seed must leave it available to expansion.

    This is the half that makes D7 worth anything: the alias is how a caller of
    the public name reaches the private implementation, and it arrives as a
    graph neighbour. Marking it seen in the seed loop would silently delete
    that path, and the retrieval benchmark would lose the point it just gained.</data>
