    <node id="sym:tests/test_answer_limits.py::test_a_body_with_no_newline_cannot_be_read_unbounded">
      <data key="d0">sym:tests/test_answer_limits.py::test_a_body_with_no_newline_cannot_be_read_unbounded</data>
      <data key="d1">symbol</data>
      <data key="d2">test_a_body_with_no_newline_cannot_be_read_unbounded</data>
      <data key="d10">test_a_body_with_no_newline_cannot_be_read_unbounded</data>
      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">tests/test_answer_limits.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">122</data>
      <data key="d13">151</data>
      <data key="d14">def test_a_body_with_no_newline_cannot_be_read_unbounded(monkeypatch, capsys):</data>
      <data key="d15">Axis 1: a response that never sends "\\n" is still bounded.

    The old line iterator had to reach EOF before yielding anything, so the
    whole body became one `bytes` object regardless of its size. Here the body
    is a single valid JSON object a full megabyte past the ceiling -- more than
    the one-block overshoot the bound allows, so an unbounded read cannot slip
    under it -- and carries no newline anywhere.</data>
      <data key="d16">true</data>
      <data key="d17">83</data>
      <data key="d_nodegraphics">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="303.00" y="2152.10" width="157.30" height="33.80" />
          <y:Fill color="#57C7E3" transparent="false" />
          <y:BorderStyle color="#4a4f57" type="line" width="1.0" />
          <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" fontSize="11" textColor="#1c2330" visible="true">test_a_body_wi…</y:NodeLabel>
          <y:Shape type="ellipse" />
        </y:ShapeNode>
      </data>
    </node>
    <node id="sym:tests/test_answer_limits.py::test_many_small_deltas_are_capped_in_total">
      <data key="d0">sym:tests/test_answer_limits.py::test_many_small_deltas_are_capped_in_total</data>
      <data key="d1">symbol</data>
