    <node id="sym:tests/test_grammar_availability.py::test_language_pack_is_capped_below_1_0">
      <data key="d0">sym:tests/test_grammar_availability.py::test_language_pack_is_capped_below_1_0</data>
      <data key="d1">symbol</data>
      <data key="d2">test_language_pack_is_capped_below_1_0</data>
      <data key="d10">test_language_pack_is_capped_below_1_0</data>
      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">tests/test_grammar_availability.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">268</data>
      <data key="d13">288</data>
      <data key="d14">def test_language_pack_is_capped_below_1_0():</data>
      <data key="d15">0.x bundles every grammar in the wheel; 1.x downloads them on first use.

    0.13.0 ships a 33 MB wheel. 1.20.0 ships 2.5 MB and an 89 KB sdist, fetching
    ~21 MB of unsigned native code from the network into the process holding the
    user's source. That contradicts the no-network guarantee in README.md and
    .github/SECURITY.md, and makes `uv.lock` and the SBOM describe a loader
    rather than what actually executes. A dependabot bump must not quietly undo
    this, so the bound is asserted rather than merely commented.</data>
      <data key="d16">true</data>
      <data key="d_nodegraphics">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="5717.38" y="3188.80" width="133.10" height="28.60" />
          <y:Fill color="#57C7E3" transparent="false" />
          <y:BorderStyle color="#4a4f57" type="line" width="1.0" />
          <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" fontSize="11" textColor="#1c2330" visible="true">test_language_…</y:NodeLabel>
          <y:Shape type="ellipse" />
        </y:ShapeNode>
      </data>
    </node>
