      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">tests/test_http_surface_removed.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">229</data>
      <data key="d13">249</data>
      <data key="d14">def test_no_module_imports_an_http_framework_or_jwt_library():</data>
      <data key="d15">No file under `repo2graph/` may import a web framework or a JWT library.

    The flag checks above only cover the two parsers. This covers the shape of
    the regression that does not go through a flag at all: a new module that
    imports `fastapi` or `jwt` and brings the transport back beside the stdio
    server rather than in place of it. It also keeps the README's and
    SECURITY.md's "no network calls" claim honest at the dependency level.</data>
      <data key="d16">true</data>
      <data key="d_nodegraphics">
        <y:ShapeNode>
