    <node id="sym:tests/test_mcp.py::_has_mcp">
      <data key="d0">sym:tests/test_mcp.py::_has_mcp</data>
      <data key="d1">symbol</data>
      <data key="d2">_has_mcp</data>
      <data key="d10">_has_mcp</data>
      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">tests/test_mcp.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">31</data>
      <data key="d13">59</data>
      <data key="d14">def _has_mcp():</data>
      <data key="d15">A real, currently-*supported* SDK is importable.

    #407/#291 dropped mcp 1.x: `serve()` now speaks only the 2.x registration
    API (`on_list_tools=`/`on_call_tool=`), so a test that drives a live
    subprocess needs mcp&gt;=2.0. This used to check
    `hasattr(Server, "list_tools")`, which is true only for the *unsupported*
    1.x generation -- so on any environment with the (now required) 2.x SDK
    installed, every test gated on it silently skipped forever. Detector:
    reverting this to the old hasattr check makes
    test_stdio_roundtrip_against_a_repo_with_no_index and
    test_stdi</data>
      <data key="d16">true</data>
      <data key="d_nodegraphics">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="3255.42" y="3475.90" width="77.40" height="27.95" />
          <y:Fill color="#57C7E3" transparent="false" />
          <y:BorderStyle color="#4a4f57" type="line" width="1.0" />
          <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" fontSize="11" textColor="#1c2330" visible="true">_has_mcp</y:NodeLabel>
          <y:Shape type="ellipse" />
        </y:ShapeNode>
      </data>
    </node>
    <node id="sym:tests/test_mcp.py::_has_any_mcp">
      <data key="d0">sym:tests/test_mcp.py::_has_any_mcp</data>
      <data key="d1">symbol</data>
      <data key="d2">_has_any_mcp</data>
      <data key="d10">_has_any_mcp</data>
      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">tests/test_mcp.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">65</data>
