      <data key="d10">test_serve_does_not_build_during_the_handshake</data>
      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">tests/test_mcp.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">1158</data>
      <data key="d13">1177</data>
      <data key="d14">def test_serve_does_not_build_during_the_handshake(mini_repo, tmp_path, monkeypatch):</data>
      <data key="d15">The build belongs on the first tool call, not before `initialize`.

    Blocking the handshake for the minute a large repo takes to parse is what
    makes a client declare the server dead, so serve() must return to its event
    loop without having touched the repo.</data>
