      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">1617</data>
      <data key="d13">1631</data>
      <data key="d14">def test_an_absurdly_long_node_id_is_clamped_before_it_reaches_the_error(mini_index):</data>
      <data key="d15">The ceiling has to bind, not merely fail to crash.

    `_str` clamps by slicing, so a 10 MB id produces a `str` and a "node not
    found" either way -- asserting only those two things passed with the clamp
    deleted. The refusal echoes the id it looked up, so the clamped length is
    observable in the output.</data>
      <data key="d16">true</data>
