      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">1634</data>
      <data key="d13">1648</data>
      <data key="d14">def test_an_absurdly_long_task_id_is_clamped_before_it_reaches_the_error():</data>
      <data key="d15">Same ceiling, same reasoning, on the task-id path.

    A real (empty) TaskManager is needed to reach the branch that echoes the id:
    with `tasks=None` the server answers "builds synchronously" and never looks
    at the id at all, which is why the previous `isinstance(out, str)` assertion
    could not see the clamp.</data>
      <data key="d16">true</data>
