    <node id="sym:tests/test_mcp.py::test_concurrent_open_index_builds_the_index_exactly_once">
      <data key="d0">sym:tests/test_mcp.py::test_concurrent_open_index_builds_the_index_exactly_once</data>
      <data key="d1">symbol</data>
      <data key="d2">test_concurrent_open_index_builds_the_index_exactly_once</data>
      <data key="d10">test_concurrent_open_index_builds_the_index_exactly_once</data>
      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">tests/test_mcp.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">1727</data>
      <data key="d13">1787</data>
      <data key="d14">def test_concurrent_open_index_builds_the_index_exactly_once(
    mini_index, mini_repo, tmp_path, monkeypatch
):</data>
      <data key="d15">Two simultaneous first calls must cost one build and share one Index.

    The HTTP transport is a `ThreadingHTTPServer` with `daemon_threads = True`,
    so two clients pointed at a server whose index does not exist yet both
    reach `open_index` before either has written anything. Unlocked, both pass
    the `not _has_index(...)` test, both parse the whole repository and then
    race each other through `atomic_write`, so the loser's work is discarded.
    The invocation count below is the detector: it reads 2 without the
    per-directory lock and 1 with it.

    `_build_index` is replaced</data>
      <data key="d16">true</data>
