      <data key="d12">1909</data>
      <data key="d13">1933</data>
      <data key="d14">def test_an_audit_record_is_written_when_the_tool_fails(mini_index, tmp_path):</data>
      <data key="d15">A failure is the case an audit trail exists for, so it must be recorded.

    `errors` level keeps only non-success outcomes, which makes this the exact
    configuration an operator would run in and the one that must not be silent.</data>
