    <node id="sym:tests/test_mcp.py::test_a_missing_index_mid_session_costs_one_call_not_the_server">
      <data key="d0">sym:tests/test_mcp.py::test_a_missing_index_mid_session_costs_one_call_not_the_server</data>
      <data key="d1">symbol</data>
      <data key="d2">test_a_missing_index_mid_session_costs_one_call_not_the_server</data>
      <data key="d10">test_a_missing_index_mid_session_costs_one_call_not_the_server</data>
      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">tests/test_mcp.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">1936</data>
      <data key="d13">1950</data>
      <data key="d14">def test_a_missing_index_mid_session_costs_one_call_not_the_server(tmp_path):</data>
      <data key="d15">One bad request must not take the stdio server down.

    `open_index` raises SystemExit when it has no index and no repo, which is
    right for the startup preflight and for a direct call. On the per-request
    path it meant an index deleted while the server ran killed the process and
    the client saw a closed pipe instead of an error. SystemExit is a
    BaseException, so an ordinary `except Exception` around the handler does not
    hold it -- this pins the conversion explicitly.</data>
      <data key="d16">true</data>
      <data key="d_nodegraphics">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="679.83" y="3691.55" width="130.07" height="27.95" />
          <y:Fill color="#57C7E3" transparent="false" />
          <y:BorderStyle color="#4a4f57" type="line" width="1.0" />
          <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" fontSize="11" textColor="#1c2330" visible="true">test_a_missing…</y:NodeLabel>
          <y:Shape type="ellipse" />
        </y:ShapeNode>
      </data>
    </node>
    <node id="sym:tests/test_mcp.py::test_audit_logging_is_off_by_default">
      <data key="d0">sym:tests/test_mcp.py::test_audit_logging_is_off_by_default</data>
      <data key="d1">symbol</data>
      <data key="d2">test_audit_logging_is_off_by_default</data>
      <data key="d10">test_audit_logging_is_off_by_default</data>
