    <node id="sym:tests/test_prod_igy.py::test_ai_text_cannot_forge_a_marker_or_a_mention">
      <data key="d0">sym:tests/test_prod_igy.py::test_ai_text_cannot_forge_a_marker_or_a_mention</data>
      <data key="d1">symbol</data>
      <data key="d2">test_ai_text_cannot_forge_a_marker_or_a_mention</data>
      <data key="d10">test_ai_text_cannot_forge_a_marker_or_a_mention</data>
      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">tests/test_prod_igy.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">606</data>
      <data key="d13">648</data>
      <data key="d14">def test_ai_text_cannot_forge_a_marker_or_a_mention():</data>
      <data key="d15">Model output is contributor-derived and rendered under the bot identity.

    Two concrete failures this prevents:
      - a second BOT_MARKER in the prose makes `comments.find()` return the
        model's text forever, so prod-igy never finds its real comment again;
      - a mention pings a real account from an App that holds issues:write.</data>
      <data key="d16">true</data>
