    <node id="sym:tests/test_prod_igy.py::test_github_app_token_is_scoped_to_the_job_permissions">
      <data key="d0">sym:tests/test_prod_igy.py::test_github_app_token_is_scoped_to_the_job_permissions</data>
      <data key="d1">symbol</data>
      <data key="d2">test_github_app_token_is_scoped_to_the_job_permissions</data>
      <data key="d10">test_github_app_token_is_scoped_to_the_job_permissions</data>
      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">tests/test_prod_igy.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">1141</data>
      <data key="d13">1169</data>
      <data key="d14">def test_github_app_token_is_scoped_to_the_job_permissions():</data>
      <data key="d15">The app token must not inherit the App installation's full permission
    grant: each `permission-&lt;name&gt;` input narrows it to something the job
    actually does, and never to more than the job's own `permissions:` block.

    `permission-issues` and `permission-checks` must NOT come back.
    `permission-*` requests that exact set and the API answers 422 "The
    permissions requested are not granted to this installation" when any one of
    them is absent from the installation's grant -- so an extra entry mints
    nothing at all rather than a slightly wider token, and the job silently falls</data>
      <data key="d16">true</data>
      <data key="d_nodegraphics">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="6134.30" y="3952.05" width="139.15" height="29.90" />
