      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">335</data>
      <data key="d13">355</data>
      <data key="d14">def test_postings_growth_from_single_char_names_is_bounded(self, tmp_path):</data>
      <data key="d15">Acceptance criterion from #378: postings count grows by less than a
        stated bound. Single-character names are drawn from
        `[A-Za-z_]`, so at most 53 distinct new postings terms
        (26 lower + 26 upper-folded-to-lower collapses to 26, + "_") can ever
        be added by this feature, regardless of corpus size -- unlike
        admitting single characters from free text, which would scale with
        the corpus.</data>
      <data key="d16">true</data>
      <data key="d17">124</data>
      <data key="d_nodegraphics">
