      <data key="d13">547</data>
      <data key="d14">def test_file_chunk0_id_matches_node_id(tmp_path):</data>
      <data key="d15">Verify file chunk 0 uses the unsuffixed node id, same as symbols.

    On main, file chunks were `file:{path}#0` while symbol chunk 0 was
    `sym:{path}::{qualname}`. A lookup for `file:notes.md` therefore missed
    chunk 0 unless the caller stripped `#0`. Multi-part splits still get
    `#1`, `#2`, … so ids stay unique and ordered.</data>
