      <data key="d14">def test_a_definition_this_file_owns_still_wins_a_bare_builtin_name(tmp_path: Path):</data>
      <data key="d15">Shadowing is only a guess *across* files.

    A `filter()` defined in the calling file, or imported into it by name, is
    what a bare `filter()` there means -- `SCOPED_CALL_KINDS` is exactly that
    set, which is why the gate reads it rather than the name alone.</data>
