      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">tests/test_secret_coverage_gaps.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">190</data>
      <data key="d13">214</data>
      <data key="d14">def test_a_pem_key_straddling_the_chunk_split_is_fully_redacted(tmp_path):</data>
      <data key="d15">The key body used to survive: only the BEGIN line matched in its slice.

    `_pem_spans` pairs a BEGIN with the next END *within the text it is given*.
    Scanning each 4,000-character slice separately left slice one matching just
    its header line and slice two -- the base64 body and the END -- matching
    nothing, so the key shipped almost whole.</data>
      <data key="d16">true</data>
