    <node id="sym:tests/test_version_surfaces.py::test_no_assertion_in_the_suite_spells_out_the_current_version">
      <data key="d0">sym:tests/test_version_surfaces.py::test_no_assertion_in_the_suite_spells_out_the_current_version</data>
      <data key="d1">symbol</data>
      <data key="d2">test_no_assertion_in_the_suite_spells_out_the_current_version</data>
      <data key="d10">test_no_assertion_in_the_suite_spells_out_the_current_version</data>
      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">tests/test_version_surfaces.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">239</data>
      <data key="d13">274</data>
      <data key="d14">def test_no_assertion_in_the_suite_spells_out_the_current_version():</data>
      <data key="d15">A test that hardcodes the version under release is red the moment the
    bump lands -- and the first run that can see it is publish.yml's `pypi`
    job, which tests the already-tagged commit.

    The bug: tests/test_export_hardening.py asserted the static `__version__`
    fallback equalled `"2.2.0"`. Nothing could fail that until a bump rewrote
    the literal it was shadowing, so it passed every PR and aborted the 3.0.0
    release after the tag was cut and the bump PR merged. The fix is to read
    the surface -- `declared_version()` here, or the literal in
    `repo2graph/__init__.py` -</data>
      <data key="d16">true</data>
      <data key="d_nodegraphics">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="951.67" y="5388.85" width="154.27" height="33.15" />
          <y:Fill color="#57C7E3" transparent="false" />
          <y:BorderStyle color="#4a4f57" type="line" width="1.0" />
          <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" fontSize="11" textColor="#1c2330" visible="true">test_no_assert…</y:NodeLabel>
          <y:Shape type="ellipse" />
        </y:ShapeNode>
      </data>
    </node>
