      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">193</data>
      <data key="d13">207</data>
      <data key="d14">def test_pointer_capture_is_released_on_both_pointerup_and_pointercancel():</data>
      <data key="d15">A capture never released swallows every later pointer event on the page.

    This is a source-level assertion rather than a DOM test: a real one needs a
    JS runtime (jsdom or playwright), and this repo has no Node toolchain in its
    dev extra. It pins the property that actually regressed -- a handler losing
    its release call -- but it cannot prove the released id matches the captured
    one. This is the one untested-in-a-browser property here.</data>
      <data key="d16">true</data>
      <data key="d_nodegraphics">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="3356.30" y="5388.85" width="130.07" height="27.95" />
